course: dictionary
lesson: 2081
title: Constructive feedback and talk
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: «Your story has a great ending. Try adding more detail to the middle.» This is constructive feedback. It says what is good, and it gives a way to make the work better.
explain: Constructive means helpful and useful, aiming to improve something. Its opposite is destructive, which breaks things down. Ask yourself: does this comment help someone build something better?
explain: Look at the word's clues. Construct means to build, so constructive means building up. «Our group had a constructive discussion, and everyone shared a good idea.» Here the talk helped the group move forward.
fact: Constructive means helpful and useful, aiming to improve something.
fact: «Constructive criticism» points out a fault and also shows how to fix it.
fact: «Constructive» comes from the idea of building, so it means building up rather than breaking down.
fact: «A constructive suggestion» is an idea that could make something better.
fact: «That is rubbish» is not helpful. «Try a brighter colour here, it would stand out more» is constructive.
exercise: «Your feedback should be constructive.» What does constructive mean? | Finished and perfect | Harsh and cruel | Very loud | *Helpful, aiming to improve
exercise: Mia says, «You missed a full stop.» Ella says, «Next time, read it aloud to catch missing full stops.» Which comment is constructive? | Both are equally rude | Neither, because feedback is never useful | *Ella, because she gives a way to improve | Mia, because she points out a mistake
exercise: Which word means the opposite of constructive, breaking things down? | *Destructive | Thoughtful | Useful | Helpful
test: «Our class had a constructive discussion about the park plan.» What does constructive mean here? | Shouting until everyone gave up | Quiet and sleepy | *Building up ideas to improve the plan | Very short and quick
test: Which is a constructive suggestion? | I don't care about your story | You always get everything wrong | Your drawing is ugly | *Try using more colour to make the sky look brighter
exam: Which sentence uses constructive correctly? | I ate a constructive sandwich for lunch | The rain was constructive all afternoon | *The coach gave constructive feedback: my kick was strong, and my stance could be wider | The coach was constructive and threw the ball at my head
